/E (Creative Types/Roles -  Creative respondents in Charlotte report working in multiple roles within the music ecosystem. The most common roles include musician or performer of original music \(56%\) and cover band performer \(39%\), followed by composer or songwriter \(34%\), music educator \(29%\), and music producer or engineer \(22%\). Additional roles reported include symphony, orchestra, chamber ensemble, or opera performers \(21%\), session musicians \(21%\), music creative directors such as conductors or music directors \(12%\), and interdisciplinary artists combining music with other art forms \(11%\). Smaller segments of respondents identify as electronic artists or DJs \(9%\) and music creative support roles \(3%\).)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
612 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /BlockQuote
/P 412 0 R
/T (Creative respondents in Charlotte report taking on a wide range of roles across the local music ecosystem, most commonly as musicians and performers of original music \(56%\) and cover bands \(39%\), followed by composers and songwriters \(34%\), music educators \(29%\), and producers or engineers \(22%\). Survey responses indicate a highly experienced creative community, with 84% of respondents reporting more than 10 years of experience. Top career concerns identified by Creative respondents include the rising cost of living and pay rates not keeping pace, with lack of consistent music work also cited as a significant concern. On average, Creative respondents report spending $6,667 annually on their music careers, contributing a collective $4.7 million in total creative spending each year, with 44% of those expenses paid locally.)
/E (Creative respondents in Charlotte report taking on a wide range of roles across the local music ecosystem, most commonly as musicians and performers of original music \(56%\) and cover bands \(39%\), followed by composers and songwriters \(34%\), music educators \(29%\), and producers or engineers \(22%\). Survey responses indicate a highly experienced creative community, with 84% of respondents reporting more than 10 years of experience. Top career concerns identified by Creative respondents include the rising cost of living and pay rates not keeping pace, with lack of consistent music work also cited as a significant concern. On average, Creative respondents report spending $6,667 annually on their music careers, contributing a collective $4.7 million in total creative spending each year, with 44% of those expenses paid locally.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
