/T (Sources of Income - Creative respondents rely primarily on local live performance as their main source of music income. Nearly half of Creative respondents \(48%\) report earning most or all of their music income from local live performance, making it the strongest income source in the local ecosystem. Teaching serves as a secondary income stream, while touring performance plays a more limited role, with 43% reporting little or no touring income. Income from songwriting, studio work, recordings, and merchandise is largely supplemental. )
/E (Sources of Income - Creative respondents rely primarily on local live performance as their main source of music income. Nearly half of Creative respondents \(48%\) report earning most or all of their music income from local live performance, making it the strongest income source in the local ecosystem. Teaching serves as a secondary income stream, while touring performance plays a more limited role, with 43% reporting little or no touring income. Income from songwriting, studio work, recordings, and merchandise is largely supplemental. )
