/T (Local Performance Pay Structure - When asked about local performance compensation, creative respondents most commonly report being paid through flat guarantees \(59%\), followed by door splits or a percentage of bar sales \(24%\). Per-service payment structures, such as rehearsal or performance fees common in ensemble or symphony work, are reported by 18% of respondents. Smaller shares report volunteer or community service performances \(11%\), unpaid or showcase performances \(6%\), or tips-only compensation \(7%\).)
/E (Local Performance Pay Structure - When asked about local performance compensation, creative respondents most commonly report being paid through flat guarantees \(59%\), followed by door splits or a percentage of bar sales \(24%\). Per-service payment structures, such as rehearsal or performance fees common in ensemble or symphony work, are reported by 18% of respondents. Smaller shares report volunteer or community service performances \(11%\), unpaid or showcase performances \(6%\), or tips-only compensation \(7%\).)
