/T (Industry Occupation -  Industry respondents report working across a wide range of music-related roles. The most commonly reported occupations include event and venue workers \(18%\) and music marketing professionals \(18%\), followed by music development \(16%\) and agents and business services \(14%\). Additional roles include recording \(11%\), production support \(9%\), and music media \(8%\). Smaller shares of respondents report working in wholesale or retail \(4%\), label or distribution \(1%\), music publishing \(1%\), and the public sector \(1%\), reflecting a broad but fragmented industry workforce.)
/E (Industry Occupation -  Industry respondents report working across a wide range of music-related roles. The most commonly reported occupations include event and venue workers \(18%\) and music marketing professionals \(18%\), followed by music development \(16%\) and agents and business services \(14%\). Additional roles include recording \(11%\), production support \(9%\), and music media \(8%\). Smaller shares of respondents report working in wholesale or retail \(4%\), label or distribution \(1%\), music publishing \(1%\), and the public sector \(1%\), reflecting a broad but fragmented industry workforce.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
