/P 418 0 R
/T (Industry respondents in Charlotte represent a diverse and multi-functional music industry workforce, led by event and venue workers \(18%\) and music marketing professionals \(18%\), followed by music development \(16%\) and agents and business services \(14%\). Respondents report a relatively balanced gender distribution, with 55% identifying as male, 43% as female, and 2% using a different term. Access to industry services relies heavily on self-management, particularly for booking \(63%\), management \(60%\), and publicity and social media \(72%\), while locally sourced services are most common for studios \(37%\) and legal or accounting services \(31%\). Industry respondents primarily serve local clients, with additional national and limited international reach.)
/E (Industry respondents in Charlotte represent a diverse and multi-functional music industry workforce, led by event and venue workers \(18%\) and music marketing professionals \(18%\), followed by music development \(16%\) and agents and business services \(14%\). Respondents report a relatively balanced gender distribution, with 55% identifying as male, 43% as female, and 2% using a different term. Access to industry services relies heavily on self-management, particularly for booking \(63%\), management \(60%\), and publicity and social media \(72%\), while locally sourced services are most common for studios \(37%\) and legal or accounting services \(31%\). Industry respondents primarily serve local clients, with additional national and limited international reach.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
