/T (Creative Access to Industry - Industry respondents access services through a mix of local providers, non-local providers, self-management, and opting out. Local services are most commonly used for studios \(37%\), legal and accounting \(31%\), and equipment \(29%\). However, a significant share of respondents report managing services themselves, particularly for publicity and social media \(72%\), booking \(63%\), and management \(60%\). For several services, including labels and publishing/licensing, many respondents report not needing these services at all.)
/E (Creative Access to Industry - Industry respondents access services through a mix of local providers, non-local providers, self-management, and opting out. Local services are most commonly used for studios \(37%\), legal and accounting \(31%\), and equipment \(29%\). However, a significant share of respondents report managing services themselves, particularly for publicity and social media \(72%\), booking \(63%\), and management \(60%\). For several services, including labels and publishing/licensing, many respondents report not needing these services at all.)
