/T (Publishing/Licensing -  41% respondents report holding intellectual property rights to their music, while 59% indicate they do not. Royalty collection methods vary, with respondents most commonly reporting BMI \(51%\) and ASCAP \(33%\), while more than a quarter \(28%\) report not collecting royalties through any organization. Licensing activity remains limited, with 44% reporting no licensing activity, while others rely on third-party providers \(30%\) or publishers and rights administrators \(25%\), indicating uneven access to music rights infrastructure.)
/E (Publishing/Licensing -  41% respondents report holding intellectual property rights to their music, while 59% indicate they do not. Royalty collection methods vary, with respondents most commonly reporting BMI \(51%\) and ASCAP \(33%\), while more than a quarter \(28%\) report not collecting royalties through any organization. Licensing activity remains limited, with 44% reporting no licensing activity, while others rely on third-party providers \(30%\) or publishers and rights administrators \(25%\), indicating uneven access to music rights infrastructure.)
