/T (Work Outside Music - 60% respondents report working outside of music, with 83% of those indicating that non-music work provides their primary source of income. Respondents cite insufficient earnings from music alone \(85%\) as the leading reason for working outside the sector, followed by access to benefits such as health insurance and retirement \(52%\), flexibility to continue pursuing music \(35%\), and career development opportunities outside of music \(35%\). These responses highlight the role of external employment in sustaining long-term participation in music careers.)
/E (Work Outside Music - 60% respondents report working outside of music, with 83% of those indicating that non-music work provides their primary source of income. Respondents cite insufficient earnings from music alone \(85%\) as the leading reason for working outside the sector, followed by access to benefits such as health insurance and retirement \(52%\), flexibility to continue pursuing music \(35%\), and career development opportunities outside of music \(35%\). These responses highlight the role of external employment in sustaining long-term participation in music careers.)
