/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 423 0 R
/T (Charlotte respondents emphasize connection, collaboration, and practical support as the most important factors for strengthening the local music ecosystem. Respondents most often prioritize access to music services and industry support \(57%\), a place to collaborate musically \(50%\), and stronger connections with other creative industries \(49%\). Venue and Presenter respondents overwhelmingly identify audience development tools as their top business need \(85%\). Across the ecosystem, only 20% of respondents report having received any form of financial assistance for music-related work. Respondents primarily learn about opportunities through social media \(71%\) and personal networks \(66%\) and identify better promotion and event awareness \(72%\) as the most effective way to increase local audience engagement.)
/E (Charlotte respondents emphasize connection, collaboration, and practical support as the most important factors for strengthening the local music ecosystem. Respondents most often prioritize access to music services and industry support \(57%\), a place to collaborate musically \(50%\), and stronger connections with other creative industries \(49%\). Venue and Presenter respondents overwhelmingly identify audience development tools as their top business need \(85%\). Across the ecosystem, only 20% of respondents report having received any form of financial assistance for music-related work. Respondents primarily learn about opportunities through social media \(71%\) and personal networks \(66%\) and identify better promotion and event awareness \(72%\) as the most effective way to increase local audience engagement.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
