/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 1978 0 R
/T (Financial Support - Only 20% of Charlotte respondents reported having received financial assistance for their music-related work. Among those who have accessed support, the most common sources include private or nonprofit grants or underwriting \(55%\), assistance from friends or family or crowdfunding \(50%\), and government grants or small business supports \(45%\). A lack of awareness of available opportunities \(53%\) was the most frequently cited barrier to accessing financial assistance, followed by limited grant-writing experience \(19%\). When asked about preferred forms of support, respondents most often favored micro-grants with less oversight \(56%\), tax breaks of any kind \(46%\), and discounted or no-cost professional services such as legal or tax preparation \(39%\).)
/E (Financial Support - Only 20% of Charlotte respondents reported having received financial assistance for their music-related work. Among those who have accessed support, the most common sources include private or nonprofit grants or underwriting \(55%\), assistance from friends or family or crowdfunding \(50%\), and government grants or small business supports \(45%\). A lack of awareness of available opportunities \(53%\) was the most frequently cited barrier to accessing financial assistance, followed by limited grant-writing experience \(19%\). When asked about preferred forms of support, respondents most often favored micro-grants with less oversight \(56%\), tax breaks of any kind \(46%\), and discounted or no-cost professional services such as legal or tax preparation \(39%\).)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6]
>>
