/T (Commercial  Workspace Status -  Charlotte respondents rely heavily on rented commercial spaces, particularly for live performance activity. Nearly three-quarters of live performance venues operate in rented facilities \(73%\), as do a majority of temporary performance spaces \(69%\). Studios, rehearsal spaces, storage, and music lesson spaces also show a relatively even split between renting and ownership. When asked about unmet workspace needs, respondents most often identified a need for live performance venues \(35%\), rehearsal space \(32%\), and studio space \(28%\), indicating continued pressure around access to affordable and appropriate music-related spaces.)
/E (Commercial  Workspace Status -  Charlotte respondents rely heavily on rented commercial spaces, particularly for live performance activity. Nearly three-quarters of live performance venues operate in rented facilities \(73%\), as do a majority of temporary performance spaces \(69%\). Studios, rehearsal spaces, storage, and music lesson spaces also show a relatively even split between renting and ownership. When asked about unmet workspace needs, respondents most often identified a need for live performance venues \(35%\), rehearsal space \(32%\), and studio space \(28%\), indicating continued pressure around access to affordable and appropriate music-related spaces.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
