/T (Despite the Charlotte music workforce having a strong foundation of experience, much of that experience remains informal and loosely connected to structured training pathways and professional associations. Most respondents report learning primarily through hands-on experience \(56%\) rather than formal education, while interest in professional development is widespread. Respondents most frequently identify marketing \(53%\), audio and video recording or engineering \(50%\), and booking, promotion, and event production \(49%\) as priority skill areas, pointing to demand for practical, career-sustaining workforce support.)
