/P 2077 0 R
/T (Regulatory Fluency - Venue/Presenter respondents encounter multiple regulatory processes when organizing live entertainment, with insurance requirements cited most frequently \(50%\). Music performance licenses and security or public safety requirements each affect nearly half of respondents \(48%\), followed closely by street or parking regulations \(46%\) and amplified sound rules \(40%\). Accessibility requirements \(38%\) and special event permitting \(35%\) further contribute to the regulatory landscape. This breadth of required processes points to challenges in regulatory fluency rather than the presence of a single prohibitive rule.)
/E (Regulatory Fluency - Venue/Presenter respondents encounter multiple regulatory processes when organizing live entertainment, with insurance requirements cited most frequently \(50%\). Music performance licenses and security or public safety requirements each affect nearly half of respondents \(48%\), followed closely by street or parking regulations \(46%\) and amplified sound rules \(40%\). Accessibility requirements \(38%\) and special event permitting \(35%\) further contribute to the regulatory landscape. This breadth of required processes points to challenges in regulatory fluency rather than the presence of a single prohibitive rule.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [5]
