/T (Financial Assistance Preferences - When asked about financial support mechanisms, venue and presenter respondents show a clear preference for tools that reduce ongoing operating costs rather than one-time relief. Micro-grants are the most frequently cited form of support \(55%\), followed by tax breaks or tax-based incentives \(39%\). Fewer respondents prioritize traditional grants or loans, suggesting that predictable, flexible assistance tied to day-to-day operations may be more impactful than competitive or administratively intensive funding programs.)
/E (Financial Assistance Preferences - When asked about financial support mechanisms, venue and presenter respondents show a clear preference for tools that reduce ongoing operating costs rather than one-time relief. Micro-grants are the most frequently cited form of support \(55%\), followed by tax breaks or tax-based incentives \(39%\). Fewer respondents prioritize traditional grants or loans, suggesting that predictable, flexible assistance tied to day-to-day operations may be more impactful than competitive or administratively intensive funding programs.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [7]
>>
