/T (Venue/Presenter Tool Preference -  Respondents consistently express interest in tools that simplify and centralize interaction with city processes. A dedicated webpage outlining current live music regulations is the most desired resource \(81%\), followed by tax discounts or incentives to host live music \(63%\). Just over half of respondents favor an online permitting and communication portal \(63%\), a single point of contact within city government \(56%\), and tiered compliance or fee structures based on scale or type of presentation \(56%\). Annual training sessions and regulatory updates are also valued \(51%\), reinforcing demand for clearer guidance, transparency, and ongoing communication.)
/E (Venue/Presenter Tool Preference -  Respondents consistently express interest in tools that simplify and centralize interaction with city processes. A dedicated webpage outlining current live music regulations is the most desired resource \(81%\), followed by tax discounts or incentives to host live music \(63%\). Just over half of respondents favor an online permitting and communication portal \(63%\), a single point of contact within city government \(56%\), and tiered compliance or fee structures based on scale or type of presentation \(56%\). Annual training sessions and regulatory updates are also valued \(51%\), reinforcing demand for clearer guidance, transparency, and ongoing communication.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [5]
>>
