/T (The Charlotte music ecosystem presents an overall positive picture of belonging and inclusivity with all measures leaning more positive than negative. A strong majority of respondents describe the local scene as safe \(90%\), non-homophobic \(86%\), and inclusive \(82%\), with many also viewing it as diverse \(67%\), non-sexist \(66%\) and cooperative \(62%\). Challenges include 46% describing the scene as as elitist and 44% as ageist. These patterns suggest legacy barriers to entry for newcomers who may include younger or less experienced and emerging talent. )
